<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15553" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄρρωστ-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥώννυμι</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>weak, sickly,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				634b14
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.465c
			</span></i>. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-τως, ἔχειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aeschin.
					2.14
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				7.12
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διακεῖσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Isoc.
					19.20
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> in moral
			sense, <i>weak, feeble,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν ψυχήν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Ap.</u>
					30
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Oec.</u>
				4.2
			</span></i>(
				Comp.
			). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρρωστότερος ἐς τὴν μισθοδοσίαν</span>
			<i>remiss</i> in payment, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				8.83
			</span></i>. [
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄ̆ρωστος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					11.206
				</span></i>
			(<i><span class="en">
				Lucill.
			</span></i>).]</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
